The direct LED path on the AYN Thor — PServerBinder resolution via
reflection, the Parcel protocol it accepts, and the SN3112 sysfs shell
format — is derived from:

  Bifrost  (Pollux-MoonBench, archived)
    https://github.com/Pollux-MoonBench/Bifrost
    tools/LedController.kt
    Copyright (C) its contributors.
    Licensed under GNU General Public License v3.0.

GTC's reimplementation in app/src/main/kotlin/jr/brian/thorhud/led/
(DirectLedDriver.kt, Sn3112) keeps only the one-shot "draw a frame on
both sticks" slice of Bifrost's controller — no master-fade baseline,
no 16 ms de-dup, no layering — because the police-light beat loop
drives the animation here.
